
== first-run setup — the consent step a customer's Mac gets, and what happens when it fails ==
  PASS  1  a customer's Mac asks, first, and one dialog at a time
          asked first; the memory and company questions both survive being deferred
  PASS  2  no terminal, no path, no version number reaches his screen
          no path, no tilde, no shell, no version, no Terminal, no input field
  PASS  3  the sheet says he still needs his own Anthropic account
          BYO-Anthropic stated, in his words, above the button
  PASS  4  each missing piece is named and explained, in his language
          two rows and a plural title and note, one row and a singular title and note
  PASS  5  a build that cannot install EXPLAINS instead of offering a button
          explained, with the party named, and no button he could press in vain
  PASS  6  a failure reaches the screen verbatim, and the sheet stays usable
          the failure is his to read, and the sheet offers the next move
  PASS  7  progress is driven by the backend's events, not by the return value
          each step announced as it started; the ending came from the backend
  PASS  8  a machine that has everything is never asked
          read, and silent
  PASS  9  the button cannot be pressed twice
          one press, one run
  PASS  10  there is exactly one run_setup call site in the shipped source
          one call site (main.js:3949) across 13 shipped UI file(s); the ordering is explicit in the source
  PASS  12  a customer's Mac is not offered voice, and is not invited to it
          voice_readiness asked; ◉ absent; the greeting names only the composer
  PASS  13  a machine that can transcribe keeps the invitation
          ◉ present and the greeting invites it
  PASS  14  a mis-aimed click cannot skip the engine
          backdrop, Escape and the panel body are all inert; only the two buttons dismiss it — and the re-add is refused across all 13 shipped UI file(s)
  PASS  15  a send with no engine names the engine and offers the install
          named, offered, his words kept, and the install runs from the offer
  PASS  16  the preview rehearses the product's own refusal, byte for byte
          three sentences, one wording, no stray spaces
  PASS  11  this suite actually checked something
          98 assertions against the real DOM under WebKit

a customer's Mac is asked once, in his language, and told the truth when it fails.
